") for v in surface['vertices']: f.write(f"v {v[0]} {v[1]} {v[2]}
") for tri in surface['triangles']: f.write(f"f {tri[0]+1} {tri[1]+1} {tri[2]+1}
") Parameters: Index Base: 1-based (standard OBJ convention). Edge Cases: Not given in the sources. Prevents local self-intersections in triangle meshes generated by Surface Nets by selecting the optimal triangulation for each non-planar quadrilateral. Choose it when sharp boundaries or edges cause arbitrary diagonal partitioning to produce intersecting triangles. Time Complexity: Not given in the sources. Memory Complexity: Not given in the sources. Strengths: Standard compatibility with rendering and geometry processing tools. Limitations: Not given in the sources. When to use: Not given in the sources. When not to use: Not given in the sources. This export method is part of a sample application provided with the SurfaceNets library. The OBJ format is a standard representation used for rendering and geometry processing. SurfaceNets for Multi-Label Segmentations with Preservation of Sharp Boundaries., https://europepmc.org/article/MED/36325473, fetched 2026-10-26 (unofficial)

