encoding degree is more effective than simply reducing MLP layers (e.g., 8 to 4 layers) in the smoothing augmentation, as smaller MLPs may still learn floaters. Simple-NeRF is part of the Simple Radiance Fields (Simple-RF) family, introduced by Nagabhushan Somraj, Sai Harsha Mupparaju, Adithyan Karanayil, and Rajiv Soundararajan in 2024. The framework is viewed as semi-supervised learning where sparse depth from Structure from Motion (SfM) provides limited depth labels. The approach of using augmented models in tandem with the main radiance field model is closest to the Dual-Student architecture [Ke et al. 2019]. Simple-RF: Regularizing Sparse Input Radiance Fields with Simpler Solutions, https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.19015v5, fetched 2026-10-27

